{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's inputs and outputs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"text-inputs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text inputs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrap a UI component with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackField"},{"type":"text","value":" and pass its emitted value to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.handleChange"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"name\" #field=\"field\">\n  <ui-text-input\n    [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n    label=\"Name\"\n    [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n    [error]=\"field.api.errors.map(errorMessage).join(', ')\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (valueChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>","lang":"html"},{"type":"code","value":"errorMessage = (error: { message: string }) => error.message","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass the current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":", not a one-time default, so the UI component remains\ndriven by form state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"checkboxes-and-switches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Checkboxes and switches"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapt the output used by the component library:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"acceptedTerms\" #field=\"field\">\n  <ui-checkbox\n    [checked]=\"field.api.value\"\n    [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (checkedChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some libraries emit a details object or a union such as\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean | 'indeterminate'"},{"type":"text","value":". Normalize it at the boundary:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<ui-checkbox\n  [checked]=\"field.api.value\"\n  (checkedChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event === true)\"\n/>","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"selects-date-pickers-and-custom-controls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selects, date pickers, and custom controls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.api.handleChange"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<ui-date-picker\n  [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n  (valueChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n/>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reuse-the-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reuse the adapter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the same wiring appears throughout the application, create an Angular\nfield component that calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectField"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ChangeDetectionStrategy, Component, input } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectField } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-text-field',\n  standalone: true,\n  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n  template: `\n    <label>\n      {{ label() }}\n      <input\n        [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n        [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n        (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n        (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n      />\n      @for (error of field.api.errors; track error) {\n        <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n      }\n    </label>\n  `,\n})\nexport class TextFieldComponent {\n  label = input.required<string>()\n  field = injectField<string>()\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Apply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack-app-field"},{"type":"text","value":" alongside the field directive so the component can\ninject its field API:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<app-text-field\n  label=\"Name\"\n  tanstack-app-field\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"name\"\n/>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackAppField"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStackField"},{"type":"text","value":", and the reusable field component in\nthe parent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../splitting-forms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splitting forms"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The repository's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/angular/basic-splitting-form"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/angular/large-form"},{"type":"text","value":" examples demonstrate this pattern with typed\nchild components."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"text-inputs","text":"Text inputs","level":2},{"id":"checkboxes-and-switches","text":"Checkboxes and switches","level":2},{"id":"selects-date-pickers-and-custom-controls","text":"Selects, date pickers, and custom controls","level":2},{"id":"reuse-the-adapter","text":"Reuse the adapter","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's inputs and outputs.\n\n## Text inputs\n\nWrap a UI component with `TanStackField` and pass its emitted value to\n`field.api.handleChange`:\n\n```html\n<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"name\" #field=\"field\">\n  <ui-text-input\n    [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n    label=\"Name\"\n    [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n    [error]=\"field.api.errors.map(errorMessage).join(', ')\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (valueChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>\n```\n\n```ts\nerrorMessage = (error: { message: string }) => error.message\n```\n\nPass the current `value`, not a one-time default, so the UI component remains\ndriven by form state.\n\n## Checkboxes and switches\n\nAdapt the output used by the component library:\n\n```html\n<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"acceptedTerms\" #field=\"field\">\n  <ui-checkbox\n    [checked]=\"field.api.value\"\n    [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (checkedChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>\n```\n\nSome libraries emit a details object or a union such as\n`boolean | 'indeterminate'`. Normalize it at the boundary:\n\n```html\n<ui-checkbox\n  [checked]=\"field.api.value\"\n  (checkedChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event === true)\"\n/>\n```\n\n## Selects, date pickers, and custom controls\n\nThe integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to `field.api.handleChange`:\n\n```html\n<ui-date-picker\n  [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n  (valueChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n/>\n```\n\nChoose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary.\n\n## Reuse the adapter\n\nWhen the same wiring appears throughout the application, create an Angular\nfield component that calls `injectField`:\n\n```ts\nimport { ChangeDetectionStrategy, Component, input } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectField } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-text-field',\n  standalone: true,\n  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n  template: `\n    <label>\n      {{ label() }}\n      <input\n        [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n        [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n        (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n        (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n      />\n      @for (error of field.api.errors; track error) {\n        <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n      }\n    </label>\n  `,\n})\nexport class TextFieldComponent {\n  label = input.required<string>()\n  field = injectField<string>()\n}\n```\n\nApply `tanstack-app-field` alongside the field directive so the component can\ninject its field API:\n\n```html\n<app-text-field\n  label=\"Name\"\n  tanstack-app-field\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"name\"\n/>\n```\n\nImport `TanStackAppField`, `TanStackField`, and the reusable field component in\nthe parent.\n\nFor the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see [Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\nThe repository's `examples/angular/basic-splitting-form` and\n`examples/angular/large-form` examples demonstrate this pattern with typed\nchild components.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: ui-libraries\ntitle: UI Libraries\n---\n\nTanStack Form is headless. UI library integration consists of adapting a\nfield's value, blur callback, change callback, invalid state, and errors to the\ncomponent's inputs and outputs.\n\n## Text inputs\n\nWrap a UI component with `TanStackField` and pass its emitted value to\n`field.api.handleChange`:\n\n```html\n<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"name\" #field=\"field\">\n  <ui-text-input\n    [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n    label=\"Name\"\n    [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n    [error]=\"field.api.errors.map(errorMessage).join(', ')\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (valueChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>\n```\n\n```ts\nerrorMessage = (error: { message: string }) => error.message\n```\n\nPass the current `value`, not a one-time default, so the UI component remains\ndriven by form state.\n\n## Checkboxes and switches\n\nAdapt the output used by the component library:\n\n```html\n<ng-container [tanstackField]=\"form\" name=\"acceptedTerms\" #field=\"field\">\n  <ui-checkbox\n    [checked]=\"field.api.value\"\n    [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n    (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n    (checkedChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  />\n</ng-container>\n```\n\nSome libraries emit a details object or a union such as\n`boolean | 'indeterminate'`. Normalize it at the boundary:\n\n```html\n<ui-checkbox\n  [checked]=\"field.api.value\"\n  (checkedChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event === true)\"\n/>\n```\n\n## Selects, date pickers, and custom controls\n\nThe integration does not require a native event. Pass the value emitted by the\ncomponent to `field.api.handleChange`:\n\n```html\n<ui-date-picker\n  [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n  (valueChange)=\"field.api.handleChange($event)\"\n  (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n/>\n```\n\nChoose a serializable form value appropriate for your application, then adapt\nthe UI library's richer object at the component boundary if necessary.\n\n## Reuse the adapter\n\nWhen the same wiring appears throughout the application, create an Angular\nfield component that calls `injectField`:\n\n```ts\nimport { ChangeDetectionStrategy, Component, input } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectField } from '@tanstack/angular-form'\n\n@Component({\n  selector: 'app-text-field',\n  standalone: true,\n  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,\n  template: `\n    <label>\n      {{ label() }}\n      <input\n        [name]=\"field.api.name\"\n        [value]=\"field.api.value\"\n        (blur)=\"field.api.handleBlur()\"\n        (input)=\"field.api.handleChange($any($event).target.value)\"\n        [attr.aria-invalid]=\"field.api.meta.isInvalid\"\n      />\n      @for (error of field.api.errors; track error) {\n        <span role=\"alert\">{{ error.message }}</span>\n      }\n    </label>\n  `,\n})\nexport class TextFieldComponent {\n  label = input.required<string>()\n  field = injectField<string>()\n}\n```\n\nApply `tanstack-app-field` alongside the field directive so the component can\ninject its field API:\n\n```html\n<app-text-field\n  label=\"Name\"\n  tanstack-app-field\n  [tanstackField]=\"form\"\n  name=\"name\"\n/>\n```\n\nImport `TanStackAppField`, `TanStackField`, and the reusable field component in\nthe parent.\n\nFor the helper types used when passing a form or field to an extracted\ncomponent, see [Splitting forms](../../../splitting-forms).\n\nThe repository's `examples/angular/basic-splitting-form` and\n`examples/angular/large-form` examples demonstrate this pattern with typed\nchild components.\n"}
